%rec: Appraisal
%doc: The archivist log: how much something matters, to whom, and why. Appended and
+ never edited; the newest appraisal of a target replaces earlier ones, and one a
+ person made or reviewed outranks a machine's. Target is DISC-ID, DISC-ID:folder/,
+ DISC-ID:folder/file (relative to data/), set:CODE or collection:CODE; a target
+ without an appraisal takes the nearest one above it (file, folder, disc, set).
+ Importance is '<level> for <audience>', one per audience; levels, most first:
+ essential (must survive: several copies, one elsewhere), important (on disc),
+ useful (on disc if there is room), incidental (everyday storage is enough).
+ Only a person can mark something incidental. Basis says why; Review is when to
+ look again. Authorship and Agent as in Event.
%mandatory: Target Date Authorship
%type: Date date
%type: Review date
%type: Authorship enum automatic suggested accepted edited human

Target: TRIP-01_2019_4
Importance: essential for self
Importance: important for family
Basis: the only photos of the trip
Date: 2026-10-04
Authorship: human
Agent: human:root
Review: 2031-10-01

